The repeal provided for in the ordinance adopting this Code shall not affect the following matters and things, and such matters and things are continued in effect to the same extent as though this Code had not been adopted:
(1) Any offense or act committed or done or any penalty or forfeiture incurred or any contract or right established or accruing before the effective date of such ordinance;
(2) Any ordinance promising or guaranteeing the payment of money for the city or authorizing the issuance of any bonds for the city or any evidence of the city's indebtedness or any contract or obligation assumed by the city;
(3) Any administrative ordinance of the city not in conflict or inconsistent with the provisions of this Code;
(4) Any ordinance fixing compensation or other benefits of officers or employees of the city;
(5) Any appropriation ordinance;
(6) Any right or franchise granted by the mayor and city council to any person, firm or corporation;
(7) Any ordinance dedicating, naming, establishing, locating, relocating, opening, closing, paving, widening, vacating or establishing the grade of any street or public way in the city, or establishing lines for building setbacks therefrom;
(8) Any ordinance amending the Charter;
(9) Any ordinance providing for local improvements or assessing taxes for such improvements;
(10) Any ordinance dedicating or accepting any plat or subdivision in the city;
(11) Any ordinance annexing property in the city;
(12) Any ordinance providing for the rezoning of property;
(13) Any ordinance not inconsistent with this Code levying, imposing or providing for collection of any tax;
(14) Any ordinance prescribing traffic regulations of specific locations, prescribing through streets, parking limitations, parking prohibitions, one-way traffic or limitations on loads of vehicles or loading zones, not inconsistent with this Code;
(15) Any ordinance fixing fees or utility rates and charges, not inconsistent with this Code;
(16) Any ordinance establishing a commission, authority or agency not inconsistent with this Code;
(17) Any resolution not inconsistent with this Code; or
(18) Any temporary ordinance or special ordinance.
(Code 1982, § 1-10)

