(a) The constituted board of ethics shall have the following duties and powers:
(1) Establish procedures, rules and regulations governing its internal organization and conduct of its affairs;
(2) Hold a hearing within 60 days after the receipt of a complaint. Failure to hold a hearing within the specified time shall result in the complaint being deferred to mayor and city council for disposition;
(3) Receive and hear complaints of violations of the standards required in this division;
(4) Make such investigation and response to a complaint as it deems necessary to determine whether any person has violated any provision of this division;
(5) Hold such hearings and make such inquiries as deemed necessary to investigate and rule upon complaints;
(6) Report its findings to the mayor and city council within five days of the completion of the hearing for such action as the mayor and city council deem appropriate.
(Ord. of 11-18-1999, art. V)

