(a) [Generally.] The provisions of this Code for general business licensing shall apply to applications for new licenses under this chapter, in addition to the following:
(1) Fee. All applications for new licenses under this chapter shall be accompanied by a payment, in cash or by certified check, for the first year's license fee in the amount as set by the mayor and city council and business taxes provided for in this Code for the classification into which the applicant falls;
(2) Additional information. The city application shall be a photocopy or other copy of all the appropriate state applications and forms, with a city supplemental application form provided by the city, as well as the following:
a. A legal description of the property upon which the proposed premises are located, together with a plat of the property by a registered land surveyor;
b. A certificate by a registered land surveyor that the proposed premises are not within 300 feet of any church or within 600 feet of any school, schoolground or college campus;
c. A current photograph of the applicant;
d. Fingerprints of the applicant, to be taken by the police department;
e. A certificate from the building inspector as to the zoning classification of the proposed premises.
(b) Oath. The application shall also contain a form of oath providing that the information disclosed in the application is true and correct and, providing further, that the applicant will abide by, observe and conduct his business according to the rules and regulations prescribed by the city, the Georgia Alcoholic Beverage Code (O.C.G.A. § 3-1-1 et seq.), as amended, and the rules and regulations of the state department of revenue in respect thereto. The oath shall be taken by the applicant and the agent in charge of the establishment, if different from, or additional to, the applicant, and the oath shall be taken by the true owners.
(c) False statement; misrepresentation. Any false statement or material misrepresentation in any application under this section shall be grounds for the revocation of any license granted under this section.
(Code 1982, § 3-54)

