(a) The clerk shall deny a city license under this chapter on any of the following grounds:
(1) Failure to meet state requirements for a state license;
(2) Failure to pay required fees and taxes;
(3) Failure to provide valid information, documents, etc., required by this chapter;
(4) False information in the application or attached documents;
(5) Improper residency of registered agents;
(6) Failure to pass review by the chief of police;
(7) Failure to post and maintain proper signs and advertisements required in this chapter;
(8) Failure to meet distance or location requirements;
(9) Prior convictions, as provided in section 10-10; or
(10) Failure to meet any other requirements in this chapter for a license of the class applied for.
(b) An application which has been denied shall not be resubmitted for a period of 12 months after the denial, unless there is a substantial change therein which would affect the reason for the original denial.
(c) The city clerk may otherwise issue any city license provided for in this chapter after approval by the city council.
(Code 1982, § 3-60)

