(a) Except as otherwise authorized by law:
(1) No person knowingly, directly or through another person, shall furnish, cause to be furnished or permit any person in such person's employ to furnish any alcoholic beverage to any person under 21 years of age;
(2) No person under 21 years of age shall purchase, attempt to purchase or knowingly possess any alcoholic beverage;
(3) No person under 21 years of age shall misrepresent such person's age in any manner whatsoever for the purpose of illegally obtaining any alcoholic beverage;
(4) No person, knowingly or intentionally, shall act as an agent to purchase or acquire any alcoholic beverage for, or on behalf of, a person under 21 years of age; and
(5) No person under 21 years of age shall misrepresent his identity or use any false identification for the purpose of purchasing or obtaining any alcoholic beverage.
(b) The provisions contained in O.C.G.A. § 3-3-23(b), (c), (d) and (e) are hereby adopted with like effect as if recited in this subsection, and any future amendment or repeal of such provisions shall amend or repeal the pertinent provisions of this section.
(Code 1982, § 3-67)
State Law reference— Similar provisions, O.C.G.A. § 3-3-23.

