(a) It shall be unlawful for any person to sell any wine or malt beverage at a place within 300 feet of any church or school within the city. Any person who shall violate this section shall, if licensed, be liable to the suspension or revocation of said license. This section shall not apply not any location for which a license has been issued prior to July 1, 1981, nor to the renewal of such license; nor shall this section apply at any location for which a new license is applied for, if the sale of the wine and beer was lawful at such location at any time during the 12 months immediately preceding such application. For the purposes of this section, the term "school" does not include college or university.
(b) Distance shall be measured in linear feet by the most direct route of travel on the ground and shall be measured in the following manner:
(1) From the front door of the structure from which malt beverages are sold or offered for sale;
(2) In a straight line to the nearest public sidewalk, walkway, street, road or highway;
(3) Along such public sidewalk, walkway, street, road or highway by the nearest route;
(4) To the front door of the church building, or to the nearest portion of the schoolgrounds, whichever is applicable.
(Code 1982, § 3-29; Res. No. 10-0415-19, 4-15-2010; Res. No. 10-0415-20, 4-15-2010)
Cross reference— Distance of distilled spirits from churches and schools, § 10-138; zoning, app. B.
State Law reference— Similar provisions, O.C.G.A. § 3-3-21.

